module gunbc.native_product_cache_seed_growth

import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

// FORWARD-FREEZE RECEIPT for the hand Rust that keys, stores and reuses the two native instruments'
// emitted products (CI programme row R3, docs/plans/ci-end-to-end-accounting.md).
//
// PURPOSE (gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing). `//gunbc/instruments:self-host` and
// `:v2-native-cli` each emit and cargo-build one closure on every required run, then run their
// door and refusal controls against the executable. The emit/build is a pure function of the six
// causal axes of v2.compiler.self_host.generation PreMaterializationIdentity, so the repeat is
// authored redundancy (DESIGN section 2). The consumer is the seed's own preparation step
// (cli_run native_lane_runner prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry): it is the only producer of these
// products today, so the keyed store lands where the production is. It serves the v2 self-host
// lane, and it is the first consumer of std.materialization_provider
// ArtifactRequest::NativeCompilerArtifactRequest.
data native_product_cache_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_product_cache", decl_name: "assemble_key", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_product_cache", decl_name: "derive_key", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_product_cache", decl_name: "lookup", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_product_cache", decl_name: "commit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run.native_product_cache", decl_name: "restore_from_shared_store", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_toolchain_identity_for_key", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host", decl_name: "probe_build_configuration_for_key", field: WholeDeclaration }
  ],
  reason: "derive_key folds the six PreMaterializationIdentity axes in declared order with SHA-256: producer_compiler is the SHA-256 of the running seed executable (/proc/self/exe) after masking every occurrence of env!(GUNBC_BUILD_IDENTITY) with a same-length placeholder (build.rs rustc-env is that one identity only; GUNBC_MATERIALIZED_TREE_IDENTITY feeds it, it is not a second embed); source_closure is the entry closure plus the census-only declaration universe at content grain; target_model is rust plus host arch/os; toolchain and build_configuration are the emitted crate's cargo identity and flags; required_lens_contract is the entry. An unreadable seed image is counted MISS cause producer_image_unreadable; empty, short, or absent identity in the image is counted MISS cause producer_identity_unmasked; never a lane refusal. Seed CI rustflags remap the checkout, isolated cargo home and rustup home from gunbc.ci_isolated_toolchain_home_layout (the same segments isolation writes into GITHUB_ENV; test.claim.toolchain_home_standing_witness.isolation_shell_and_seed_remap_share_the_isolated_home_layout). Byte-identity of two remapped seed builds is a remote measurement, not a floor claim; lookup serves an entry only after re-hashing the executable against its manifest and the manifest against the key, and refuses (never deletes: a read does not mutate the store) any entry that disagrees; commit writes a private sibling directory and renames it, and publication is admitted only for a merge_group run whose red+restore completed (publication_admitted). Executed controls: seed unit tests (hit under the key and miss under a changed one, corrupted executable refused and left in place, entry without the red refused, every measured input reaches the key through assemble_key, the fold derive_key uses, only_a_completed_red_on_the_merge_queue_publishes, producer_axis is the sha256 of the masked running executable, a changed seed image moves the producer digest). restore_from_shared_store runs only on an L1 miss and only when a read credential is present; every failure is a named NativeProductRestoreUnavailable cause counted as a MISS, and a restored entry still passes lookup's re-hash. The per-host root is bound on pull requests and merge_group; because a per-host directory is writable by PR-controlled code it is not the wall. The wall is the shared R2 store with credential asymmetry (gunbc.native_product_shared_store): the read token reaches same-repo pull requests and the queue, the write token only a merge_group-pinned federation (gunbc.native_product_federation). No CI saving is claimed until the operator has run gcp_iam_converge and a cross-host HIT is measured.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete these items when the native ancestry lane makes std.materialization_provider provider_serve the only producer of the native compiler artifact, serving it through a read-back digest of the executable and a request_key over the same six axes. A provider that keys but does not verify the executable on read would satisfy a trigger naming only the key while a corrupted store entry is still served.",
  current_boundary: "Reachable only from prepare_emitted_compiler_for_entry, and only when GUNBC_NATIVE_CACHE_ROOT names a store; with it unset nothing is read or written. Writes only under <root>/native-products. CONSUMER (§3c, consumed in this change): the emit-build job reads the shared R2 store through restore_from_shared_store (spawning gunbc.native_product_shared_transfer native_product_restore_wet) on same-repo pull requests and the merge queue, and the merge queue publishes admitted entries through native_product_save_wet; the cache-blobs tokens are pinned in r2_origin fabric_cache_blobs_standing and emit-build carries id-token: write with the two WIF steps. Residual: the GCP service accounts and the write pool exist only after the operator runs gcp_iam_converge; until then the auth steps fail soft as counted MISSes. The per-host directory realization remains the L1 beneath the shared tier, and the provider_serve deletion trigger above applies after it."
}
